# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight. Size: every excluded path is one the daemon
# does not have to receive before the first instruction runs. Correctness: a
# host artefact copied into an image silently shadows the one the build was
# supposed to produce — a stale web/dist embedded instead of the freshly
# compiled SPA, a host-built binary of the wrong architecture, or a developer's
# live database shipped to a registry.
#
# Patterns are matched against the path from the context root, and `*` does not
# cross a `/` — so `**/` is used wherever a name can occur at any depth.

# Build output. web/dist is rebuilt in the node stage and copied across
# explicitly; node_modules is reinstalled from package-lock.json, and the host's
# copy is both large and, on a mac, the wrong platform's binaries.
bin/
web/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Local runtime state. A developer's database and evidence must never end up in
# an image — see docs/deploy.md for where the container keeps its own.
**/*.duckdb
**/*.duckdb.wal
**/*.duckdb.tmp/
evidence/

# Local configuration and secrets. The container is configured through the
# environment; a baked-in .env would override it invisibly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# History. The build stamps its version through --build-arg (see the Makefile's
# docker-build target), so it never needs to run git.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Test, coverage and editor noise. The end-to-end suite drives the image's
# binary from outside it; nothing in the image runs Playwright.
**/*.out
coverage/
e2e/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.devcontainer/

# Documentation and the backlog: nothing in the image reads them, and a docs
# edit should not invalidate a build layer. deploy/ is *not* excluded — the
# entrypoint and health-check scripts are copied from it.
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
